-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- interval terms in normal form
-- an interval term is kept as a join of meets of literals, each literal a number (four times the
-- variable's number, plus 2 for a variable introduced by quotation, plus 1 for a reversed one), a
-- meet a list of literals in increasing order, the join a list of meets in order with none
-- containing another; so two interval terms equal in the algebra have one form. The empty join is
-- the end 0 and the join of the empty meet is the end 1
nk-code : NkTm → Word
nk-code (nk-num c) = c
nk-code t = #0
